# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
# LEADING SLASH. Written as `build/` this matches a directory called build at
# ANY depth, which meant bpcad/build/ - the compiler, the helpers and every
# template, 3104 lines and the entire geometry engine - was silently untracked
# for the whole life of the repo. Three commits shipped a package that could
# not build anything. Anchor it to the top level.
/build/
/dist/

# Generated part output. spec.yaml, report.md, run.json and regression.json
# ARE tracked - they are the durable record. The meshes are rebuilt from the
# spec in seconds and would otherwise churn the history on every build.
parts/*/out/
# AND under a version folder. `parts/*/out/` matches parts/birdhouse/out/ and
# not parts/birdhouse/v02/out/, so every refinement's meshes leaked back in -
# a 39 MB STL was staged before anyone noticed. Same class of mistake as the
# `build/` rule above: a pattern that looked right for the layout it was
# written against and not for the one that grew.
parts/*/*/out/

# The original drop of the reference material. reference/ holds a byte-identical
# copy, is read-only, and is what the tests and templates actually use. Keeping
# both in the repo would only create doubt about which one is canonical.
files/

# `bpcad render` writes here when it is run from the repo root - it defaults to
# ./out relative to the working directory, not to the part's own folder. Every
# other generated mesh is already ignored under parts/; this one was not, and
# sat staged waiting to be committed by accident.
/out/

# IMPORTED AND UPLOADED FILES. `library/` is where an STL somebody brought in
# lands, along with reference photos posted to /api/upload. It is a person's
# working material on their own machine, not part of the program, and one
# uploaded phone photo would put a stranger's picture in the repository.
/library/

# Generated brand assets. bpcad_media/build/ is 46 files derived from
# icon-master.svg by build_brand.py, and a derived file in version control is
# a file that will disagree with its source. The SOURCE is tracked; run
# `python bpcad_media/build_brand.py` to make the rest.
#
# The exception is what the clients actually ship, which IS tracked:
# bpcad/web/static/icons/, the iOS asset catalogue and the Android mipmaps.
# Those are inputs to a build, not outputs of one.
/bpcad_media/build/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
